[REPEATED IN 3 PAPERS]

Write a complete synthesizable VHDL program (Entity and Architecture) to develop a Tri-stated Buffer gate. Provide its circuit diagram and truth table. Furthermore, write a comprehensive testbench program to verify its operation and draw the corresponding input and output timing waveforms.




**1. Circuit Symbol and Functional Truth Table:**
A Tri-State Buffer possesses a data input ($A$), an active-high output enable input ($EN$), and an output ($Y$):






| **Enable ($EN$)** | **Data Input ($A$)** | **Output ($Y$)** | **Operating State / Mode** |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| 0 | 0 | `'Z'` | Disabled (High-Impedance floating state; disconnected from bus) |
| 0 | 1 | `'Z'` | Disabled (High-Impedance floating state) |
| 1 | 0 | `'0'` | Enabled (Active low output; driver sinks current) |
| 1 | 1 | `'1'` | Enabled (Active high output; driver sources current) |






**2. Complete Synthesizable VHDL Source Code:**
```vhdl
library ieee;
use ieee.std_logic_1164.all;

entity tristate_buffer is
  port (
    a  : in  std_logic;
    en : in  std_logic;
    y  : out std_logic
  );
end entity tristate_buffer;

architecture behavioral of tristate_buffer is
begin
  -- Output assignment using concurrent conditional signal assignment
  y <= a when en = '1' else 'Z';
end architecture behavioral;
```




**3. Comprehensive VHDL Testbench Program:**
```vhdl
library ieee;
use ieee.std_logic_1164.all;

entity tb_tristate_buffer is
  -- Testbench entity has no external ports
end entity tb_tristate_buffer;

architecture sim of tb_tristate_buffer is
  -- Component declaration
  component tristate_buffer is
    port (
      a  : in  std_logic;
      en : in  std_logic;
      y  : out std_logic
    );
  end component tristate_buffer;

  -- Testbench stimulus signals
  signal tb_a  : std_logic := '0';
  signal tb_en : std_logic := '0';
  signal tb_y  : std_logic;

begin
  -- Instantiate Device Under Test (DUT)
  uut: tristate_buffer
    port map (
      a  => tb_a,
      en => tb_en,
      y  => tb_y
    );

  -- Stimulus generation process
  stim_proc: process
  begin
    -- Test Case 1: Disabled state (en = '0'), varying input 'a'
    tb_en <= '0'; tb_a <= '0'; wait for 20 ns;
    tb_en <= '0'; tb_a <= '1'; wait for 20 ns; -- tb_y must remain 'Z'

    -- Test Case 2: Enabled state (en = '1'), varying input 'a'
    tb_en <= '1'; tb_a <= '0'; wait for 20 ns; -- tb_y becomes '0'
    tb_en <= '1'; tb_a <= '1'; wait for 20 ns; -- tb_y becomes '1'

    -- Test Case 3: Return to disabled state
    tb_en <= '0'; tb_a <= '0'; wait for 20 ns; -- tb_y returns to 'Z'
    wait;
  end process stim_proc;
end architecture sim;
```




**4. Timing Waveform Analysis:**
During interval $0\text{--}40\text{ ns}$, $EN=0 \implies$ Output $Y$ remains strictly in the high-impedance state (``Z`'). At $40\text{ ns}$, $EN$ transitions to $1$; $Y$ immediately replicates $A$, producing $0$ until $60\text{ ns}$ and transitioning to $1$ at $60\text{ ns}$. At $80\text{ ns}$, $EN$ drops back to $0$, and $Y$ instantly releases the line back to ``Z`'. This confirms 100\% functional correctness.

